cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "aircombat-bench: A Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning Benchmark for 3-D Air Combat"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-06"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AhmetYldz39/aircombat-bench"
authors:
  - family-names: "Yıldız"
    given-names: "Ahmet"
    email: "ahmetstar150@gmail.com"
abstract: >
  aircombat-bench is an open-source benchmark for multi-agent reinforcement
  learning in 3-D air combat. It provides a 6-DoF F-16 simulation (JSBSim
  aerodynamic coefficients, RK4 integration), a 2v2 dogfighting environment
  with a weapons effects zone (WEZ) model, and six trained baselines
  (MAPPO, MAPPO+GAT, MAPPO+GAT+OM+Role, QMIX, FACMAC, FACMAC+OM+R).
  All baselines are evaluated at 500 episodes with a fixed seed for
  reproducibility. The best baseline (FACMAC+OM+R) achieves 84.2% win rate
  against a rule-based heuristic opponent.
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - multi-agent
  - air combat
  - simulation
  - MAPPO
  - QMIX
  - FACMAC
